<title>PORTUGAL: Petrogal plans 25 bln esc bond.</title>
<headline>Petrogal plans 25 bln esc bond.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese state-controlled oil company Petrogal-Petroleos de Portugal has issued the mandate for the organisation of an 25 billion escudo ($163 million) bond, one of the banks involved announced.</p>
<p>Petrogal has awarded the mandate to Banco Espirito Santo (BES), Banco Mello de Investimentos (BMI) and Banco Totta &amp; Acores (BTA), Banco Mello said in a statement.</p>
<p>It gave no further details of the proposed bond.</p>
<p>Spain's Argentaria will take part as senior co-leader, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
